local.launch.consent.access=The program can list the agents and their models, start a session with its own prompt, follow its sessions, and open them. An open brings the IDE to the front. Allow keeps the permission. Allow Once keeps it until the IDE restarts.
local.launch.consent.access.once.only=The program can list the agents and their models, start a session with its own prompt, follow its sessions, and open them. An open brings the IDE to the front. It runs scripts or commands that can change after your answer, so Allow Once is the only permission. It lasts until the IDE restarts.
local.launch.consent.full.access=The registry key air.local.launch.full.access is on. So the program can also start a session with full access, in which the agent runs commands and changes files without asking you.
